<section class="section">
  <div class="container article-body" style="max-width:920px;">
    <h2>What Makes the Dairy Queen Snickers® Blizzard an All-Time Candy Classic?</h2>
    <p>Among Dairy Queen's permanent candy-bar lineup, the Snickers® Blizzard® Treat easily claims the title of the most texturally diverse. While single-note mix-ins like chocolate chips or cookies provide uniform bites, Snickers brings four distinct elements into play: crunchy roasted peanuts, gooey ribbons of caramel, pillowy sweet nougat, and smooth milk chocolate.</p>
    <p>When blended into cold vanilla soft serve at high spindle speed, the Snickers bar shatters into a satisfying spectrum of textures. Fine chocolate flecks infuse the soft serve with rich cocoa notes, while larger morsels of peanut and chilled caramel maintain their chew and satisfying bite, delivering a full candy-bar experience in every spoonful.</p>

    <h2>2026 Prices &amp; Calorie Counts Across All Cup Sizes</h2>
    <p>The Snickers Blizzard is priced within Dairy Queen's standard year-round treat tier, making it one of the most accessible candy Blizzards on the menu:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Mini ($3.49 · ~320 cal):</strong> An ideal post-lunch portion with just enough candy crunch to satisfy your sweet tooth without overindulging.</li>
      <li><strong>Small ($4.49 · 500 cal · 18g Fat):</strong> The most popular single-serving size, striking an optimal balance between rich mix-ins and creamy soft serve.</li>
      <li><strong>Medium ($5.49 · ~700 cal):</strong> Generously loaded with Snickers pieces, perfect for a mid-afternoon treat or dessert companion.</li>
      <li><strong>Large ($6.49 · ~1,050 cal):</strong> A massive 21-ounce indulgence packed with roasted peanuts and chilled caramel.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Candy Bar Face-Off: Snickers vs. Other DQ Classics</h2>
    <p>Choosing between Dairy Queen's iconic candy Blizzards comes down to your preferred balance of crunch, salt, and chocolate depth:</p>
    <div class="table-wrap"><table class="size-table"><thead><tr><th>Blizzard Treat</th><th>Mini Price</th><th>Small Cal</th><th>Key Mix-Ins &amp; Texture Profile</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Snickers® Blizzard</strong></td><td class="price-cell">$3.49</td><td>500</td><td>Roasted peanuts, chewy caramel, nougat, milk chocolate shards</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Reese's® Peanut Butter Cup</strong></td><td class="price-cell">$3.99</td><td>600</td><td>Creamy peanut butter cups; saltier, intensely chocolate-PB focused</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Butterfinger® Blizzard</strong></td><td class="price-cell">$3.49</td><td>470</td><td>Crispety, crunchety peanut butter wafer shards; drier crisp texture</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Turtle Pecan Cluster</strong></td><td class="price-cell">$3.99</td><td>570</td><td>Buttery roasted pecans, warm caramel, rich chocolate cone dip pieces</td></tr></tbody></table></div>

    <h2>Customization Hacks &amp; Allergy Precautions</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>The Double-Chocolate Upgrade:</strong> Ask the crew to blend in a pump of hot fudge (~$0.50) along with your Snickers pieces for an ultra-rich, fudge-drenched sundae flavor.</li>
      <li><strong>Extra Peanuts:</strong> If you enjoy high-contrast crunch, ask for an extra scoop of Spanish peanuts or extra Snickers pieces.</li>
      <li><strong>Severe Allergy Advisory:</strong> The Snickers Blizzard contains both peanuts and dairy, and Dairy Queen stores utilize shared blending equipment. Guests with severe peanut or tree-nut allergies should avoid this item; consider the <a href="/items/oreo-blizzard">Oreo Blizzard</a> or soft serve cones instead.</li>
      <li><strong>Upside-Down Guarantee:</strong> DQ guarantees every Blizzard is thick enough to hold upside down before it reaches your hands—if your server forgets the flip, your next Blizzard is free.</li>
    </ul>

